+# Employers and insurers
+*Part of the [B2B2C research](/wiki/b2b2c). Sources: 49, from the notes in `docs/research/research_notes/Aurelia B2B2C models and plan/`.*
+
+This page covers selling Aurelia through employers, employee assistance programmes (EAPs), insurers and health systems: how these buyers pay, what they demand, and what happened to the companies that sold to them. Research was collected on 2026-11-23. Most findings come from search summaries, not full pages, so single-source numbers are leads to check.
+
+Labels used on this page: **(measured)** is a peer-reviewed or survey measurement. **(company claim)** is a vendor's own marketing or price page. **(third-party estimate)** is an aggregator or analyst figure, not audited. **(trade press)** is a news report. **(estimate)** is our own inference.
+
+## In one minute
+
+- **The realistic price anchor for a content-only app is $50–70 per employee per year.** Calm Teams and Wysa are the only public prices. Clinical-care vendors charge more but bundle coaching and therapy.
+- **Uptake is low.** EAP use is about 2–3% of eligible staff. Among employees who enrolled in one digital benefit, only 38% used the self-guided tools.
+- **Buyers now demand proof.** Large employers review vendors on dashboards and say vendors must "demonstrate value or face replacement". A pilot with activation and retention data is the entry ticket.
+- **Insurers bundle wellness apps as perks, not as reimbursed care.** Kaiser says Calm and Headspace are not covered benefits and may be discontinued at any time. Real reimbursement (Germany's DiGA) needs medical-device status and clinical evidence.
+- **The incumbents were repriced hard.** Headspace is being sold for up to $300M after a $3B merger valuation. Pear Therapeutics went from a $1.6B valuation to a $6.05M asset sale because payers would not pay.
+- **For Aurelia now:** a self-serve team tier and small pilots, not enterprise or payer deals.
+
+## How employer vendors sell
+
+Employer mental-health vendors almost never publish prices. Sales are by quote. Two structures dominate (Headspace, 2024-07-18, company claim) [Headspace pricing models](https://organizations.headspace.com/blog/evaluating-mental-health-solution-pricing-models):
+
+- **Single fee per employee per month (PEPM):** one fee for all eligible staff covers app access plus a set number of coaching or clinical sessions.
+- **Lower base PEPM plus use:** app access at a low PEPM, with coaching, therapy and psychiatry billed per use.
+
+Headspace's example contract runs three years. It says competitors "charge in the double digits per member per month" (company claim, same page).
+
+### Published prices and scale
+
+| Vendor | Price or scale | Date | Label | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Calm Teams (5–300 seats) | About $70 per seat per year (about $5.83/month), paid upfront; custom quote above 300 seats | 2026 | third-party estimate; tier confirmed on Calm's pages | [FrontDeskReview](https://frontdeskreview.com/software/meditation-apps/calm/); [Calm Teams](https://www.calm.com/teams) |
+| Wysa for Work | $50 per employee per year, code-based access | Undated page | company claim | [Wysa for Work](https://www.wysa.com/wysa-for-work-copy) |
+| Calm Health (enterprise) | Quote only | Current page | company | [Calm Health employers](https://health.calm.com/employers/) |
+| Unmind | Pricing on request, no free plan | Undated | third-party | [G2](https://www.g2.com/products/unmind/pricing) |
+| Lyra | Valued about $5.6B (Series F, January 2022); $100M revenue disclosed in January 2021 | 2021–2022 | third-party estimate | [Multiples.vc](https://multiples.vc/private-comps/lyra-health) |
+| Spring Health | Valued $3.3B (Series E, July 2024); implied revenue about $125M | 2024 | third-party estimate | [Multiples.vc](https://multiples.vc/private-comps/spring-health) |
+| Modern Health | Passed $1B valuation with a $74M round | 2021-02-16 | trade press | [STAT](https://www.statnews.com/2021/02/16/soaring-mental-health-unicorns-race-to-meet-employer-needs/) |
+| Calm Health reach | More than 17M people (June 2025); more than 39M (January 2026) | 2025–2026 | company claim via analyst | [Sacra](https://www.sacra.com/c/calm) |
+
+"Covered lives", as in Calm Health's figures, measures eligibility, not use (estimate). Aurelia should not quote reach without activation beside it.
+
+A content-only app sits in the Calm Teams and Wysa band, roughly $4–6 per seat per month paid annually (estimate). It does not sit in the "double digits" band, which pays for coaching and therapy.
+
+## Activation and engagement
+
+There is no standard benchmark, and published numbers mix three denominators: eligible, enrolled and active employees.
+
+| Finding | Figure | Denominator | Date | Label | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Used any self-directed digital resource in one employer benefit | 38% of 950; about 44% never used the app | Enrolled | 2024 | measured, peer-reviewed | [JMIR 2024](https://jmir.org/2024/1/e48696) |
+| EAP utilisation across seven regions | About 2–3% | Eligible | Undated | third-party estimate (Gallup, cited by Spring Health; original not verified) | [Spring Health](https://www.springhealth.com/blog/how-innovative-eaps-drive-utilization) |
+| Employers reporting high / moderate / low EAP use | 38% / 37% / 25% | Employers | 2025 | measured survey (Arizent/EBN, in a Teladoc paper) | [Teladoc / EBN](https://www.teladochealth.com/content/dam/tdh-www/us/en/documents/white-paper/EBN_Teledoc%20Health_WhitePaper.pdf) |
+| McDonald's Singapore adoption of the Intellect app | 28% | Not stated | Undated | company claim | [Intellect](https://intellect.co/read/workplace-wellbeing-in-singapore-asean/) |
+| Singapore employees using no mental-health tool in the past year | 55% | Employees | Fieldwork Dec 2024–Jan 2025 | measured survey | [Intellect × Milieu](https://intellect.co/read/intellectxmilieuinsightreport_pressrelease/) |
+| Large US employers seeing higher mental-health use | 73% | Employers | 2025 | measured survey (Business Group on Health) | [US Chamber, 2025-10-31](https://www.uschamber.com/health-care/employers-remain-committed-to-offering-robust-health-coverage-enhance-offerings-and-access) |
+| Employer mental-health spending | Fell 7% despite higher use | — | 2025 | trade press | [Insurance Business](https://www.insurancebusinessmag.com/us/news/benefits/mental-health-utilization-is-up--but-employer-spending-fell-7-in-2025-587992.aspx) |
+
+Priced per eligible seat, low activation would not cost revenue in year one. It would make renewal hard once the buyer checks a dashboard (estimate). Aurelia's one-sentence start and daily check-in are its plausible activation advantages, but that is untested.
+
+## What buyers demand
+
+### Proof of value
+
+- Business Group on Health: "Vendors and programs must demonstrate value or face replacement." Its 2025 well-being survey found employers would use dashboards to evaluate vendors, and 100% include mental health in their strategy (measured survey, 2025). [BGH 2025 survey](https://www.businessgrouphealth.org/Newsroom/News-and-Press-Releases/Press-Releases/2025-Employer-Well-being-Strategy-Survey)
+- Employers projected a 9% cost increase for 2026 (trade press). [Fierce Healthcare](https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/payers/employers-brace-9-cost-increase-2026-business-group-health-survey). BGH's August 2026 survey projects a median 9.2% rise for 2027 (measured survey). [BGH 2027 summary](https://www.businessgrouphealth.org/-/media/bgh/images/2027-employer-healthcare-strategy-survey/2027_hcs_survey-es-final.pdf)
+
+Cost pressure plus dashboards means a vendor without usage data is the first one cut (estimate).
+
+### Security, compliance and evidence
+
+| Requirement | Who shows it | Label | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| ISO 27001 | Unmind (enterprise page) | company claim | [Unmind Enterprise](https://unmind.com/enterprise) |
+| ISO 27001 and ISO 27701 | Wysa (UK G-Cloud 14 listing) | company claim on a government marketplace | [UK Digital Marketplace](https://www.applytosupply.digitalmarketplace.service.gov.uk/g-cloud/services/987715074233145) |
+| SOC 2 | No public evidence found for either vendor | — | — |
+| UK NHS: DTAC approval plus NHS Talking Therapies assessment | Required for digital therapies | regulator | [NICE HTE9](https://nice.org.uk/guidance/hte9/resources/digitally-enabled-therapies-for-adults-with-anxiety-disorders-early-value-assessment-pdf-1396179075013) |
+| Clinical evidence | NICE found "not enough clinical evidence" on Wysa, Iona Mind and Minddistrict; research use only | regulator | [NICE HTE8](https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/HTE8/chapter/3-committee-discussion) |
+
+**Minimum kit for a first employer pilot (estimate):**
+
+- a security and privacy pack: GDPR (or Indonesia's PDP Law), a data-processing agreement, and an ISO 27001 or SOC 2 roadmap;
+- an aggregate, anonymised engagement dashboard, never individual mood data (see [Claims and regulation](/wiki/b2b2c/regulation));
+- a crisis-escalation policy.
+
+Direct employer deals for a content-only product can likely avoid US HIPAA "covered entity" duties; health-plan deals pull HIPAA in. This is our inference; confirm with counsel. Clinical claims would push Aurelia towards medical-device rules, which it is not ready for.
+
+## Insurers and payers
+
+US payers mostly bundle wellness apps as no-cost extras outside the insured benefit. That is a fixed-fee licence, not reimbursement.
+
+| Payer or scheme | What it does | Date | Label | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Kaiser Permanente | Calm and Headspace at no added cost; 90 days a year of Headspace coach texting; ages 13+. The apps "are not covered under your health plan benefits… and may be discontinued at any time" | Current pages | company terms | [Kaiser self-care apps](https://healthy.kaiserpermanente.org/health-wellness/mental-health/tools-resources/digital) |
+| UnitedHealthcare | Offered Calm Health to more than 13M commercial members | 2024 (search summary; primary article not fetched) | trade press | [MobiHealthNews](https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/calm-expands-mental-health-support-app-internationally) |
+| Headspace and Medicare | Not a direct Medicare/Medicaid provider; in-network with select Medicare Advantage plans | Current | company | [Headspace help](https://help.headspace.com/hc/en-us/articles/37974782380827-Can-I-use-Headspace-therapy-if-I-have-Medicare-or-Medicaid) |
+| Headspace direct-to-consumer insured therapy | Typical copays $0–35 per session | 2025-06-18 | trade press | [HIT Consultant](https://hitconsultant.net/2025/06/18/headspace-launches-insurance-covered-therapy-direct-to-consumers) |
+| Headspace for Cigna Healthcare | Launched | 2025-11-10 | trade press | [HIT Consultant](https://hitconsultant.net/2025/11/10/headspace-for-cigna-healthcare-enhances-everyday-mental-health-support) |
+| Calm Health | Launched for payers, providers and self-insured employers | 2022-10-18 | trade press | [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2022/10/18/calm-launches-clinical-mental-health-offering-calm-health/) |
+
+### Germany's DiGA: real reimbursement, high bar
+
+| Measure | Figure | Date | Label | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| DiGA listed | 58 (48 permanent, 10 provisional) | End of 2025 | official report | [GKV-Spitzenverband DiGA report 2025](https://www.gkv-spitzenverband.de/media/dokumente/krankenversicherung_1/telematik/digitales/2025_DiGA_Bericht_GKV_SV.pdf) |
+| Dispensed; spending | About 1.6M; about €400M | End of 2025 | official report | [GKV-Spitzenverband](https://www.gkv-spitzenverband.de/media/dokumente/krankenversicherung_1/telematik/digitales/2025_DiGA_Bericht_GKV_SV.pdf) |
+| Prescriptions activated | About 1.9M since 2020, 82% activated | Current page | insurer data | [AOK](https://www.aok.de/pp/gg/daten-und-analysen/digitale-gesundheitsanwendungen/) |
+| Average price | €541 per prescription (range €119–2,077, usually per 90 days); about 50% lower after negotiation, median €221 | 2024 | measured, peer-reviewed | [JMIR 2024](https://www.jmir.org/2024/1/e59013) |
+| Payer view | "Rising costs with little benefit" | 2025-04-02 | insurer statement | [GKV-SV press release](https://www.gkv-spitzenverband.de/gkv_spitzenverband/presse/pressemitteilungen_und_statements/pressemitteilung_2011904.jsp) |
+
+DiGA needs CE/MDR medical-device certification, a clinical study and a German launch (estimate from the scheme rules). That path does not fit Aurelia's wellness, non-clinical positioning.
+
+In the US, Medicare does not cover prescription digital therapeutics, and commercial payers hesitate. This was a central cause of Pear's failure (trade press). [In Vivo / Citeline](https://invivo.pharmaintelligence.informa.com/IV147722/Pear-Bankruptcy-Filing-Highlights-Reimbursement-Barriers-for-Digital-Therapeutics)
+
+## Health systems and the NHS
+
+The NHS route for mental-health apps runs through NICE early value assessments and NHS Talking Therapies. Even Wysa is rated "research only" (regulator, [NICE HTE8](https://nice.org.uk/guidance/hte8/chapter/2-The-technology)). NICE's first rapid healthtech guidance recommended four digital tools for children and young people with mild-to-moderate anxiety or low mood, conditional on DTAC (regulator). [NICE news](https://nice.org.uk/news/article/digital-mental-health-tech-for-children-and-young-people-recommended-by-nice-in-first-rapid-healthtech-guidance)
+
+In the US, Calm Health partners with LifeStance to route users with complex needs to clinical care (trade press). [MobiHealthNews](https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/calm-health-lifestance-health-partner-users-complex-mental-health-needs). No sourced evidence was found of health systems paying for general wellness apps at scale.
+
+Health systems are a stage-3 channel at best (estimate). Social prescribing of a wellness app is plausible as an unpaid recommendation, not paid procurement. A clinical route would also make Aurelia a medical device.
+
+## Why the incumbents struggled
+
+| Company | What happened | Date | Label | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Headspace | Merged with Ginger at about $3B | October 2021 | trade press | [MobiHealthNews](https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/headspace-health-confirms-second-round-layoffs-less-year) |
+| Headspace | Laid off about 50 (Dec 2022), 181 or about 15% (mid-2023), about 13% (Nov 2024); staff therapists moved to contract roles from 2025-03-15 | 2022–2025 | trade press | [Becker's](https://beckershospitalreview.com/digital-health/headspace-lays-off-181-employees-in-2nd-round-of-job-cuts.html); [eMarketer](https://www.emarketer.com/content/headspace-cuts-13--of-its-workforce--transitions-staff-therapists-contract-part-time-roles) |
+| Headspace | Sword Health agreed to buy it, all cash, "up to $300M"; close expected early Q4 2026 | 2026-09-17 | trade press | [HLTH](https://hlth.com/insights/news/sword-to-acquire-headspace-in-deal-worth-up-to-300m) |
+| Calm | Last disclosed valuation $2B | December 2020 | third-party | [CB Insights](https://www.cbinsights.com/company/calmcom/financials) |
+| Calm | Estimated ARR about $450M (2021) falling to about $300M (2022–2023) | 2021–2023 | third-party estimate, conflicting on timing | [Sacra](https://www.sacra.com/c/calm) |
+| Pear Therapeutics | Bankrupt April 2023; assets sold for $6.05M against about $32M debt and a $1.6B valuation two years earlier | 2023-05-22 | trade press | [Axios Pro](https://www.axios.com/pro/health-tech-deals/2023/05/22/pear-therapeutics-sold-6m-four-parts) |
+
+From the $3B merger value to at most $300M is a write-down of 90% or more (estimate; the two deals are not like for like).
+
+**Lessons (estimate):**
+
+1. Do not build a model that needs reimbursement before payer-grade evidence exists (Pear).
+2. Avoid fixed clinical-labour costs before revenue (Headspace's therapist layoffs).
+3. Large buyers are consolidating towards platforms that bundle care. A content-only app should sell cheaply and self-serve, or partner into a platform or EAP as content.
+4. Activation and retention data from a real pilot are the currency for every channel.
+
+Sword buying Headspace for its "AI care" positioning is weak evidence that acquirers value AI-personalised delivery.
+
+## Southeast Asia and Indonesia
+
+| Finding | Figure | Date | Label | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
